@startuml Domain4_PromptEngineering
' ============================================================
'  CCA-F  |  DOMAIN 4 — PROMPT ENGINEERING
'  Activity diagram: every lesson shown as a step in ONE
'  worked example — an invoice-extraction pipeline.
'  Each node carries: PURPOSE + EXAMPLE from that lesson.
' ============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FDFDFB
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E8F0FE
  BorderColor #4A6FA5
  BorderThickness 1.3
  FontColor #1A2B45
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  DiamondBorderColor #E8A33D
  DiamondFontColor #5A3E1B
  StartColor #2E7D32
  EndColor #B23B3B
  BarColor #4A6FA5
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDF3
skinparam noteBorderColor #D9C88A
skinparam partitionBorderColor #B0BEC5

title **CCA-F · Domain 4 — Prompt Engineering**\nOne pipeline, every topic: building a reliable invoice-extraction system

start

' ================= BUILD THE PROMPT =================
partition "**A · Structure the Prompt**" {

  :**XML Tags to Structure Prompts**;
  note right
    **Purpose:** unambiguous open/close boundaries the
    model is trained to respect — beats markdown/dashes.
    **Example:** wrap the job in <instructions>, the invoice
    in <document_content>, samples in <examples>.
    **Trap:** tags are clarity, NOT injection defence.
  end note

  :**Document Structure Patterns**\n(multi-part tasks);
  note right
    **Purpose:** each source gets its own labelled block so
    output can be attributed to the right document.
    **Example:** <document index="1"><source>ACME.pdf</source>
    <document_content>…</document_content></document>.
    **Trap:** attribution is a STRUCTURE problem, not model size.
  end note
}

' ================= EXAMPLES / FEW-SHOT =================
partition "**B · Teach by Example**" {

  if (Output varies\nand instructions\ncan't fix it?) then (yes)
    :**Why Examples Work**\n(pattern matching + format anchoring);
    note right
      **Purpose:** an example fixes format, tone, reasoning
      & scope at once; anchors the FIRST output token.
      **Example:** show one filled invoice→JSON pair.
      **Trap:** few-shot = 2+; more is NOT linearly better.
    end note

    :**Designing High-Quality\nFew-Shot Examples**;
    note right
      **Purpose:** examples must mirror real production
      inputs; put the BEST example LAST (recency weight).
      **Example:** 3 diverse invoices incl. 1 edge case
      (missing PO number).
      **Trap:** contamination — fix by REMOVING the bad
      example, never by instructing around it.
    end note
  else (no — well-defined task)
    :Stay **zero-shot**\n(clear instructions only);
  endif
}

' ================= REASONING DEPTH =================
partition "**C · Control Reasoning**" {

  if (Task needs\nmulti-step\nreasoning?) then (yes)
    :**Chain-of-Thought**\n(visible reasoning in the prompt);
    note right
      **Purpose:** elicitation phrase IS the mechanism —
      "think step by step" before answering.
      **Example:** reason about tax lines before totalling.
      **Trap:** lives in PROMPT TEXT, no API flag; and it
      does NOT help creative / simple-lookup tasks.
    end note

    if (Prompt-level CoT\nnot enough?) then (escalate)
      :**Extended Thinking**\n(thinking parameter, adaptive+effort);
      note right
        **Purpose:** internal reasoning via API; set type
        =adaptive, effort low→medium→**high(default)**→x-high→max.
        **Example:** raise effort for a 40-line invoice with
        split shipments.
        **Trap:** thinking tokens are BILLED + count against
        context; max_tokens caps thinking+output TOGETHER.
      end note
    else (no)
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
}

' ================= STEERING OUTPUT =================
partition "**D · Steer the Output**" {

  :**Steering Model Output**\n(supersedes Prefilling);
  note right
    **Purpose:** on 4.6+ flagships prefilling → HTTP 400.
    Steer via system prompt / structured outputs / strict tools.
    **Example:** set tone + format defaults in system prompt;
    put "just this once, as a table" in the user turn.
    **Trap:** Prefill still works on pre-4.6 (Haiku 4.5) —
    NOT a blanket removal. Don't oversteer (conflicting signals).
  end note

  note left
    **Prefilling** (legacy): partial assistant turn commits the
    first token. Format-anchoring ONLY — never refusal bypass.
  end note

  :**Temperature / top_p / top_k**\n(legacy sampling);
  note right
    **Purpose:** old dials for randomness; current models
    REJECT non-default values with a 400 error.
    **Example:** instead of temp 0, ask plainly for
    "consistent, deterministic" extraction.
    **Trap:** temp 0 was never a universal safe default.
  end note
}

' ================= CONVERSATION MGMT =================
partition "**E · Manage the Conversation**" {

  if (Task ambiguous, staged,\nor needs human review?) then (yes)
    :**Multi-Turn Interactions**;
    note right
      **Purpose:** dialogue beats one prompt when ambiguous,
      interdependent, review-gated, or too long.
      **Example:** one clarifying turn — "Which currency?" —
      before extracting.
      **Trap:** ask ONE targeted question, not an intake form.
    end note

    :**Conversation State &\nContext Management**;
    note right
      **Purpose:** manage accumulation, drift, noise.
      **Example:** re-anchor framing each turn; partial reset
      carrying only key decisions forward.
      **Trap:** reset BEFORE the window truncates silently.
    end note
  else (no — single call)
  endif
}

' ================= STRUCTURED OUTPUT =================
partition "**F · Guarantee the Shape**" {

  :**JSON Mode /\nStructured Outputs**;
  note right
    **Purpose:** constrained decoding guarantees schema-valid
    JSON during generation — no parse/retry loop.
    **Example:** format.type=json_schema + your invoice schema.
    **Trap:** guarantees CONTAINER, not judgment.
  end note

  :**Schema Design for\nReliable Extraction**;
  note right
    **Purpose:** required vs optional + precise descriptions
    drive correct values.
    **Example:** mark PO optional (not every invoice has one);
    describe "total = grand total incl. tax".
    **Trap:** required field with no data → hallucinated value.
  end note

  :**Structured Outputs Limits**;
  note right
    **Purpose:** only an enforceable SUBSET compiles; SDK
    transforms the rest (strip→fold into description→validate).
    **Example:** maximum:100 not enforced by decoding; enum is.
    **Trap:** request-wide caps — 20 strict tools, 24 optional
    params, 16 union params.
  end note

  :**Tool Definitions for\nStructured Data**\n(strict tool use);
  note right
    **Purpose:** strict:true guarantees tool-call ARGUMENTS
    match the input schema (name, types, required present).
    **Example:** record_invoice(vendor, total, due_date) as a
    tool call — no string to parse.
    **Trap:** structured outputs shapes the TEXT reply;
    strict tools shape the ARGUMENTS. Often use BOTH.
  end note
}

' ================= VALIDATION =================
partition "**G · Validate & Retry**" {

  :**Validation Loops &\nHallucination Prevention**;
  note right
    **Purpose:** extract→validate→re-prompt on failure (loop),
    plus grounding to stop confabulation.
    **Example:** re-include the invoice text; correct ONLY the
    failing field; cite the source line per field.
    **Trap:** validating at the END with no re-prompt path;
    temperature reduction does NOT fix grounding gaps.
  end note

  :**Validation Gates &\nRetry Strategy**;
  note right
    **Purpose:** gates decide pass/block; bounded retries with
    backoff avoid infinite loops.
    **Example:** stop after N retries → route to human review.
  end note

  ' ---- the two guarantee gaps every schema lesson warns about ----
  if (Check **stop_reason** first) then (refusal / max_tokens)
    :Handle exception\n(refusal = 200 + refusal;\nmax_tokens = truncated JSON);
    note right
      **Trap (repeated across lessons):** schema guarantee
      BREAKS on a safety refusal or a max-tokens cutoff.
      Always check stop_reason before trusting the payload.
    end note
    :Re-prompt / raise limit\n**(loops back to validate)**;
    note right #FFE0E0
      Red path = retry loop back into
      the validation step above.
    end note
  else (ok)
  endif

  if (All validation\nlayers pass?) then (no)
    #FFE0E0:Targeted re-prompt\n(specific error + source text)\n**(loops back to validate)**;
  else (yes)
  endif
}

' ================= MULTI-PASS =================
partition "**H · Review**" {

  if (High-stakes output?) then (yes)
    :**Multi-Pass Review**\n(one pass isn't enough);
    note right
      **Purpose:** separate passes each catch a different
      error class — generate, then critique, then refine.
      **Example:** pass 2 checks totals add up; pass 3 checks
      values match the source.
      **Trap:** stacking passes on low-stakes work = wasted cost.
    end note
  else (no)
  endif
}

:**Reliable structured JSON**\nready for the downstream pipeline;

stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#E8F0FE>| Topic / activity |
  |<#FFF3E0>| Decision point |
  |<#FFE0E0>| Failure → retry |
  **Read top-to-bottom:** each partition (A–H) is a phase of
  Domain 4; the red arrows are the validation retry loops.
endlegend

@enduml
